    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plācāmentum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				means of pacifying</i> or <i>appeasing</i>, <i>a lenitive</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc veluti placamento terrae blandiuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 7, 19, § 42</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deŭm placamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 1, 63</span></i>.</div>
